'''Ronto Grill''' was a [[restaurant]] located at [[the wharf]], a part of [[Level 1313]] on the [[planet]] [[Coruscant]]. It featured a large [[Foodstuff|food]] court and signage with the name of the establishment written in [[Aurebesh]]. It was named after the [[ronto]],<ref name="Gone" /> a pack animal of [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Databank-Ronto">{{Databank|ronto|Ronto|quote=Gentle and strong, rontos are favored pack animals for Tatooine's Jawas.}}</ref>

==History==
After narrowly averting a disaster with some [[Type II loadlifter droid|binary loadlifters]] that she was repairing for a customer, [[Rafa Martez]] promised to meet her sister [[Trace Martez|Trace]] at [[the wharf]]. Trace then headed to Ronto Grill with [[Ahsoka Tano]], where the two talked over a meal of [[space waffle]]s. Rafa later met them there, revealing that she had sold the [[droid]]s to [[Lokann]] despite knowing that the loadlifter was dangerous, which Tano and Trace were not pleased about. However, Rafa countered that she used the [[Currency|money]] to pay off the sisters' debts to [[Pintu Son-El]]. Tano then decided to leave the restaurant early to repair her [[Joben T-85 speeder bike|speeder bike]]. Before leaving, Trace thanked Tano for saving her earlier and left with her to help her in her repairs.<ref name="Gone" />

Several decades later, Ronto Grill was advertised on the chassis of [[R4-G77]], an [[astromech droid]] owned by [[Hype Fazon]], a [[racer]] [[pilot]] on the ''[[Colossus]]'' [[Fuel|refueling]] [[Space station|station]].<ref name="SW-Designing Star Wars: Star Wars Resistance">{{SW|url=news/designing-star-wars-resistance|text=Designing ''Star Wars'': ''Star Wars Resistance''|author=[[Kristin Baver]]|date=2019-03-11}} {{C|Slide 12}}</ref>

